Hi

Please excuse my lack of VAX / VMS knowledge before I explain my problem
!

I am a research associate at Imperial College and I have a 12 inch
philips LM1200 OD which contains x-ray ct data from a siemans HiQ ct
scanner from india. I have no other info and assume that it was a VAX
driven OD read/writer system written using siemans proprietry format.

I can see the ct elbow images from the OD on a similar scanner at a
london hospital but cannot transfer the data to another media as the
scanner is not networked or connected to a CD read/writer.

Recently we tried reading the OD at another london hospital which has a
philips scanner and OD read/writer driven by VAX/VMS. We could dump data
from the OD when we mounted it as foreign otherwise we could not access
any data. However the VAX system has limited memory and the full
capacity of the OD would be very much above that limit. Ideally we only
want to dump those blocks which contain image data. We dumped about
23,000 blocks of data which consisted mostly of large blocks of 0s or 2s
I think and there was a 'parity error' message with each block. Although
at the beginning of the dump we did see the name of the hospital and a
volume number description among the data.

Does anyone know how to make the OD device 'native' or someway of
interogating the file system / structure so we can copy/dump the image
dataset ? One colleague thinks that we may need to first recover the
image data as it could be a backup. If anyone has experience of these
issues or can help with getting the data out then please contact me
a.s.a.p.

many thanks
bal
